#, xml-text
msgid "Linux PAM Dependencies"
msgstr "Dependências do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid "Optional"
msgstr "Opcionais"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:101
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libnsl\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"rpcsvc-proto\"/>, &berkeley-db;, <ulink "
"url=\"https://github.com/linux-audit/audit-userspace\">libaudit</ulink>, and"
" <ulink url=\"https://github.com/openSUSE/libeconf\">libeconf</ulink>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"libnsl\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"rpcsvc-proto\"/>, &berkeley-db;, <ulink "
"url=\"https://github.com/linux-audit/audit-userspace\">libaudit</ulink> e "
"<ulink url=\"https://github.com/openSUSE/libeconf\">libeconf</ulink>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:109
#, xml-text
msgid "Optional (To build the Documentation and Man Pages)"
msgstr "Opcionais (Para construir a Documentação e Páginas de Manual)"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:111
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"docbook5\"/>, <xref linkend=\"docbook-xsl-ns\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"fop\"/> (for the PDF format), <xref linkend=\"libxslt\"/>, and "
"<xref linkend='lynx'/> (for the plain text format)"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"docbook5\"/>, <xref linkend=\"docbook-xsl-ns\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"fop\"/> (para o formato PDF), <xref linkend=\"libxslt\"/> e <xref "
"linkend='lynx'/> (para o formato de texto simples)"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:120
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"shadow\"/> <phrase revision=\"systemd\"> "
"and <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> must</phrase><phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">must</phrase> be reinstalled and reconfigured after "
"installing and configuring <application>Linux PAM</application>."
msgstr ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"shadow\"/> <phrase revision=\"systemd\"> e "
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> precisa</phrase><phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">precisa</phrase> ser reinstalado e reconfigurado depois de"
" instalar e de configurar o <application>Linux PAM</application>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:128
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"With Linux-PAM-1.4.0 and higher, the pam_cracklib module is not installed by"
" default. Use <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> to enforce "
"strong passwords."
msgstr ""
"Com o Linux-PAM-1.4.0 e superior, o módulo pam_cracklib não é instalado por "
"padrão. Use <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> para impor "
"senhas fortes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:137
#, xml-text
msgid "Kernel Configuration"
msgstr "Configuração do Núcleo"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:140
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For the PAM module <filename class='libraryfile'>pam_loginuid.so</filename> "
"(referred by the PAM configuration file <filename>system-session</filename> "
"if <phrase revision='sysv'><xref linkend='elogind'/> is "
"built</phrase><phrase revision='systemd'><xref linkend='systemd'/> is "
"rebuilt with PAM support</phrase> later) to work, a kernel configuration "
"parameter need to be set or the module will just do nothing:"
msgstr ""
"Para o módulo PAM <filename class='libraryfile'>pam_loginuid.so</filename> "
"(referido pelo arquivo de configuração PAM <filename>system-"
"session</filename>, se <phrase revision='sysv'><xref linkend='elogind'/> for"
" construído</phrase><phrase revision='systemd'><xref linkend='systemd'/> for"
" reconstruído com suporte a PAM</phrase> posteriormente) funcionar, um "
"parâmetro de configuração do núcleo precisa ser configurado ou o módulo "
"simplesmente não fará nada:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:160
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Linux PAM"
msgstr "Instalação do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:163
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you've installed <xref linkend='docbook5'/>, <xref linkend='docbook-xsl-"
"ns'/>, <xref linkend='libxslt'/>, and <xref linkend='lynx'/> and you wish to"
" generate the plain text format of the documentations, modify "
"<filename>meson.build</filename> to use <xref linkend='lynx'/> instead of "
"W3m or Elinks that BLFS does not provide:"
msgstr ""
"Se você tiver instalado <xref linkend='docbook5'/>, <xref linkend='docbook-"
"xsl-ns'/>, <xref linkend='libxslt'/> e <xref linkend='lynx'/> e desejar "
"gerar o formato de texto simples das documentações, modifique "
"<filename>meson.build</filename> para usar <xref linkend='lynx'/> em vez de "
"W3m ou Elinks que o BLFS não fornece:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:171
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -e \"s/'elinks'/'lynx'/\"                       \\\n"
"    -e \"s/'-no-numbering', '-no-references'/      \\\n"
"          '-force-html', '-nonumbers', '-stdin'/\" \\\n"
"    -i meson.build</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed -e \"s/'elinks'/'lynx'/\"                       \\\n"
"    -e \"s/'-no-numbering', '-no-references'/      \\\n"
"          '-force-html', '-nonumbers', '-stdin'/\" \\\n"
"    -i meson.build</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:177
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Compile and link <application>Linux PAM</application> by running the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Compile e vincule o <application>Linux PAM</application> executando os "
"seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:181
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..        \\\n"
"  --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"  --buildtype=release \\\n"
"  -D docdir=/usr/share/doc/Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..        \\\n"
"  --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"  --buildtype=release \\\n"
"  -D docdir=/usr/share/doc/Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:192
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, a suitable <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> "
"configuration file must exist."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, um arquivo de configuração adequado "
"<filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> precisa existir."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><caution><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:197
#, xml-text
msgid "Reinstallation or Upgrade of Linux PAM"
msgstr "Reinstalação ou Atualização do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:199
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have a system with Linux PAM installed and working, be careful when "
"modifying the files in <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d</filename>, "
"since your system may become totally unusable. If you want to run the tests,"
" you do not need to create another <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> "
"file. The existing file can be used for the tests."
msgstr ""
"Se você tiver um sistema com Linux PAM instalado e funcionando, seja "
"cuidadoso(a) ao modificar os arquivos em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d</filename>, pois seu sistema possivelmente se"
" torne totalmente inutilizável. Se você deseja executar os testes, [então] "
"não precisa criar outro arquivo <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename>. O "
"arquivo existente pode ser usado para os testes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:218
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For a first-time installation, create a configuration file by issuing the "
"following commands as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"Para uma primeira instalação, crie um arquivo de configuração emitindo os "
"seguintes comandos como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:223
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -m755 -d /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>auth     required       pam_deny.so\n"
"account  required       pam_deny.so\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_deny.so</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -v -m755 -d /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>auth     required       pam_deny.so\n"
"account  required       pam_deny.so\n"
"password required      pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_deny.so</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:233
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now run the tests by issuing <command>ninja test</command>.  Be sure the "
"tests produced no errors before continuing the installation."
msgstr ""
"Agora execute os testes emitindo <command>ninja test</command>. Certifique-"
"se de que os testes não produziram erros antes de continuar a instalação."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:239
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For a first-time installation, remove the configuration file created earlier"
" by issuing the following command as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Para uma primeira instalação, remova o arquivo de configuração criado "
"anteriormente emitindo o seguinte comando como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:244
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>rm -fv /etc/pam.d/other</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>rm -fv /etc/pam.d/other</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:247
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the &root; user:"
msgstr "Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:250
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ninja install &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ninja install &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:253
#, xml-text
msgid "Now remove an unneeded directory as &root;:"
msgstr "Agora remova um diretório desnecessário como &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:255
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>rm -rf /usr/lib/systemd</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>rm -rf /usr/lib/systemd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:257
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you do not have the optional dependencies installed to build the "
"documentation and downloaded the optional pre-built documentation, again as "
"the &root; user:"
msgstr ""
"Se você não tiver as dependências opcionais instaladas para construir a "
"documentação e baixou a documentação opcional pré construída, novamente como"
" o(a) usuário(a) &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:261
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>tar -C / -xvf ../../Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-docs-"
"version;-docs.tar.xz</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>tar -C / -xvf ../../Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-docs-"
"version;-docs.tar.xz</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:272
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Linux-PAM"
msgstr "Configurando Linux-PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:275
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Files"
msgstr "Arquivos de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:278
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>/etc/security/*</filename> and <filename>/etc/pam.d/*</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<filename>/etc/security/*</filename> e <filename>/etc/pam.d/*</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:283
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/security/*"
msgstr "/etc/security/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:287
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/pam.d/*"
msgstr "/etc/pam.d/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:293
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr "Informação de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:296
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Configuration information is placed in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d/</filename>.  Here is a sample file:"
msgstr ""
"A informação de configuração é colocada em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d/</filename>. Aqui está um arquivo de amostra:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:301
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth            required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"account         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"session         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"password        required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/other</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal># Início /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth            required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"account         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"session         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"password        required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"\n"
"# Fim /etc/pam.d/other</literal>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:311
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now create some generic configuration files.  As the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, crie alguns arquivos genéricos de configuração. Como o(a) usuário(a) "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:315
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-account &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-account\n"
"\n"
"account   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-account</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-auth &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-auth\n"
"\n"
"auth      required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-auth</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-session\n"
"\n"
"session   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-session</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-password &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-password\n"
"\n"
"# use yescrypt hash for encryption, use shadow, and try to use any\n"
"# previously defined authentication token (chosen password) set by any\n"
"# prior module.\n"
"password  required    pam_unix.so       yescrypt shadow try_first_pass\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-password</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-account &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-account\n"
"\n"
"account   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-account</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-auth &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-auth\n"
"\n"
"auth      required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-auth</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-session\n"
"\n"
"session   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-session</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-password &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-password\n"
"\n"
"# Use resumo 'yescrypt' para encriptação; use sombra e tente usar\n"
"# qualquer token de autenticação previamente definido (senha escolhida)\n"
"# configurado por qualquer módulo anterior.\n"
"password  required    pam_unix.so       yescrypt shadow try_first_pass\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-password</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:353
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you wish to enable strong password support, install <xref "
"linkend=\"libpwquality\"/>, and follow the instructions on that page to "
"configure the pam_pwquality PAM module with strong password support."
msgstr ""
"Se você deseja ativar o suporte a senhas fortes, [então] instale <xref "
"linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> e siga as instruções naquela página para "
"configurar o módulo PAM pam_pwquality com suporte a senhas fortes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:360
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, add a restrictive <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> configuration "
"file.  With this file, programs that are PAM aware will not run unless a "
"configuration file specifically for that application exists."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, adicione um arquivo de configuração "
"<filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> restritivo. Com esse arquivo, os "
"aplicativos que reconhecem o PAM não serão executados, a menos que exista um"
" arquivo de configuração específico para esse aplicativo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:366
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth        required        pam_warn.so\n"
"auth        required        pam_deny.so\n"
"account     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"account     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"password    required        pam_warn.so\n"
"password    required        pam_deny.so\n"
"session     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"session     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/other</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Início /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth        required        pam_warn.so\n"
"auth        required        pam_deny.so\n"
"account     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"account     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"password    required        pam_warn.so\n"
"password    required        pam_deny.so\n"
"session     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"session     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# Fim /etc/pam.d/other</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:382
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <application>PAM</application> man page (<command>man pam</command>) "
"provides a good starting point to learn about the several fields, and "
"allowable entries. The Linux-PAM System Administrators' Guide at "
"<filename>/usr/share/doc/Linux-PAM-1.7.0/Linux-PAM_SAG.txt</filename> is "
"recommended for additional information."
msgstr ""
"A página de manual do <application>PAM</application> (<command>man "
"pam</command>) fornece um bom ponto de partida para aprender a respeito dos "
"diversos campos e entradas permissíveis. O Guia Linux-PAM do(a) "
"Administrador(a) do Sistema em <filename>/usr/share/doc/Linux-"
"PAM-1.7.0/Linux-PAM_SAG.txt</filename> é recomendado para informações "
"adicionais."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><important><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:392
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You should now reinstall the <xref linkend=\"shadow\"/> <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">package.</phrase> <phrase revision=\"systemd\"> and <xref "
"linkend=\"systemd\"/> packages.</phrase>"
msgstr ""
"Você agora deveria reinstalar <phrase revision=\"sysv\">o pacote</phrase> "
"<phrase revision=\"systemd\"> os pacotes <xref linkend=\"systemd\"/> "
"e</phrase> <xref linkend=\"shadow\"/>."

